#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064045 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064163 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e901ea71-aeab-5e95-939e-2401558aa708" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Global Extrema of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "69180c3b-7c26-5e5f-8d7a-42aed98431bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-3736" :question/problem "Find the global extrema of $f(x) = 2x - x^2$  on the interval $[-1,4].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=2x-x^2,$ we get\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 2-2x,\n$$\n\nand solving $f'(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n2-2x = 0 \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad x=1.\n$$\n\nThe critical points are $x=1$ and the endpoints $x=-1,4$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =2(-1)-(-1)^{2}=-3 \\\\ f(1) & =2(1)-(1)^{2}=1 \\\\ f(4) & =2(4)-(4)^{2}=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(1)=1,$ so the global maximum value is $1.$\n\n- The least value is $f(4)=-8,$ so the global minimum value is $-8.$\n\n![](images/c2/c277beb3423cc80d3ac2a001ac1063059b645c65fc8cb77978050f3831274b31.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064046 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2106ea68-f48f-5372-87c0-fa8126509655" :knowledge-point/title "Discarding Stationary Points of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "a0f47cd2-ea8f-5278-ab67-46ecd65d2f4d" :question/math-academy-id "e-3737" :question/problem "Find the global maximum and minimum values for the function $f(x) = x^4 - 6 x^2$ on the closed interval $[-1, 3].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=x^4 - 6x^2,$ we get\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 4x^3 - 12x,\n$$\n\nand solving $f'(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-12x & =0 \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-3) & =0 \\\\ 4x(x+\\sqrt{3})(x-\\sqrt{3}) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\pm \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x = -\\sqrt 3 \\approx -1.73$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,3]$, we ignore this point.\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=0,\\sqrt{3}$ and the endpoints $x=-1,3$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\nFinally, we evaluate $f$ at the critical points:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tf(-1) \t& = (-1)^4 - 6(-1)^2 = -5\\[5pt]\n \t\tf(0) \t\t& = (0)^4 - 6(0)^2 = 0\\[5pt]\n \t\tf(\\sqrt 3) \t& = (\\sqrt 3)^4 - 6(\\sqrt 3)^2 = -9\\[5pt]\n \t\tf(3) \t\t& = (3)^4 - 6(3)^2 = 27 \\\t\t\n \t\t}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the global maximum is $27$ and the global minimum is $-9.$\n\n![](images/74/74ce5114dbc93035b0be078be12149cced66ce881dfbc37768ed9febcdfcba87.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064163 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e901ea71-aeab-5e95-939e-2401558aa708" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Global Extrema of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69c09760-2d64-5dc1-bd95-dbf93b49b75e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450156} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb90533-2e1f-508d-a49f-33cb04df8165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeb90533-2e1f-508d-a49f-33cb04df8165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450157} :answer-field/id #uuid "352f6126-fd80-562e-ba27-8dfb9087ceab" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451032} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1840414b-3944-5796-ad10-fefa18374ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450158} {:answer/id #uuid "f592a2fd-2ad2-5a64-b1a1-518ee0502f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f592a2fd-2ad2-5a64-b1a1-518ee0502f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450159} :answer-field/id #uuid "9362b5d3-3ec4-5533-9758-c6204cf9b6e0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73a31074-4dac-5fd9-8605-009d13ebe2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450160} {:answer/id #uuid "8df65c50-3dc4-5365-8556-462f00971dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73a31074-4dac-5fd9-8605-009d13ebe2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450160} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c12c083-9778-5df4-89ea-8b2c7152665c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7e9580a2-179f-5d46-9d50-b4d9da5c57d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-20976" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-24x+5,$ defined on the closed interval $-2\\le x\\le 2,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The global maximum value is $45$\n- **II.** The global minimum value is $-14$\n- **III.** The global maximum value is $18$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-24x+5,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x-24,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x-24 & =0 \\\\ 12({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x-2) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x-2 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+2)-(x+2) & =0 \\\\ (x+2)({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,-1,\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=-2,\\,-1,\\,1,$ and the endpoints $x=-2,2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =3(-2)^{4}+8(-2)^{3}-6(-2)^{2}-24(-2)+5=13 \\\\ f(-1) & =3(-1)^{4}+8(-1)^{3}-6(-1)^{2}-24(-1)+5=18 \\\\ f(1) & =3(1)^{4}+8(1)^{3}-6(1)^{2}-24(1)+5=-14 \\\\ f(2) & =3(2)^{4}+8(2)^{3}-6(2)^{2}-24(2)+5=45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(2)=45,$ so the global maximum is $45.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(1)=-14,$ so the global minimum is $-14.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"\n\n![](images/9b/9b48417439d0e018250328b92561732dd9f4c8bbec157daf33287b20dac7c41f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064163 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e901ea71-aeab-5e95-939e-2401558aa708" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Global Extrema of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efae998e-dc98-5b4b-ab4c-fc5995e8225f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450322} {:answer/id #uuid "f590a205-708b-5611-9105-ca206b5a0c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f590a205-708b-5611-9105-ca206b5a0c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450323} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dcbac18-fb46-5ad0-9978-9ee853a593d3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451115} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6755131-f931-5ec0-be6b-249ba3d2433f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450324} {:answer/id #uuid "f53f5ec6-26c9-594b-a1c5-a57d8d135618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6755131-f931-5ec0-be6b-249ba3d2433f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450324} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3ebb718-81c2-5711-9fd5-d99025583547" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96fe261b-8924-5702-a08e-d644aaad551a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450326} {:answer/id #uuid "a6882046-d109-5fb1-9023-719192f9eec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96fe261b-8924-5702-a08e-d644aaad551a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450326} :answer-field/id #uuid "88b0c550-4739-517c-9c4a-5a5b493dbbd4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d406ba45-2233-5b01-8129-dbf69421606e" :question/math-academy-id "q-22568" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x},$ defined on the interval $[\\frac{1}{2},2],$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The global maximum value is $\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}$\n- **II.** The global minimum value is $2\\sqrt{e}$\n- **III.** The global minimum value is $4\\sqrt[4]{e}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot x-{e}^{x}\\cdot 1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(x-1)}{{x}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{e}^{x}(x-1)}{{x}^{2}}=0\\,⟹\\,x=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=1,$ and the endpoints $x=\\frac{1}{2},2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{{e}^{1/2}}{(\\frac{1}{2})}=2\\sqrt{e}≈3.3 \\\\ f(1) & =\\frac{{e}^{1}}{1}=e≈2.7 \\\\ f(2) & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}≈3.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(2)=\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2},$ so the global maximum is $\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(1)=e,$ so the global minimum is $e.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"\n\n![](images/98/98156f05b9b6c71c7e5a5753d024d0851a0a779741545ba2d62d3d63af41e824.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2106ea68-f48f-5372-87c0-fa8126509655" :knowledge-point/title "Discarding Stationary Points of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18996592-be0a-51dd-9117-033672b3f9f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290735} {:answer/id #uuid "3c104fc1-c554-59a0-bfd2-40ebef8d2d72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290880} {:answer/id #uuid "6b033f37-22e7-523a-baac-63d05f3ee654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291091} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc16273-b0c3-5d3e-ada8-6f51530d1b3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291156} {:answer/id #uuid "958b3c28-fb33-5d0f-a319-72156a7d2c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bc16273-b0c3-5d3e-ada8-6f51530d1b3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291156} :answer-field/id #uuid "91075236-9924-59d0-8be0-f3ed9e73279b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9c0cbdb-b0ad-5562-a0b0-37a865ff6d3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-2689" :question/problem "Find the global minimum value of the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{2}$ on the closed interval $-3\\le x\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3}-16x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-16x & =0 \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ 4x(x-2)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,0,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-3,1]$, the critical points are $x=-2,0,$ and the endpoints $x=-3,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =(-3)^{4}-8(-3)^{2}=9 \\\\ f(-2) & =(-2)^{4}-8(-2)^{2}=-16 \\\\ f(0) & =(0)^{4}-8(0)^{2}=0 \\\\ f(1) & =(1)^{4}-8(1)^{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-3)=9,$ so the global maximum is $9.$\n\n- The least value is $f(-2)=-16,$ so the global minimum is $-16.$\n\n![](images/e5/e57ff9bc04fb9d9db592dda6aac9c364fd5f2e6fcd52968627b1e0271919f5bb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2106ea68-f48f-5372-87c0-fa8126509655" :knowledge-point/title "Discarding Stationary Points of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a8313dd-5fdd-5c81-a1b5-48c8c4a34af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290805} {:answer/id #uuid "33ed80ac-0b34-5d04-b4be-e2a0347c210b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290842} {:answer/id #uuid "4a244d28-9365-55e7-81e4-fdf02c2a2c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290940} {:answer/id #uuid "6c95327d-f3a6-5aaa-8c47-7b4e3d402e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291099} {:answer/id #uuid "76c4c7f4-f5c8-5499-94aa-d57c71cb7050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76c4c7f4-f5c8-5499-94aa-d57c71cb7050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291138} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1d95fed-6abb-5898-9ccd-fc77f7d79a43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c8383b31-3ef6-56e1-8528-1bcdbd1b3b84" :question/math-academy-id "q-2721" :question/problem "Find  the global minimum value of the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+3$ on the closed interval $-1\\le x\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =12{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 12{x}^{2}(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,1]$, the critical points are $x=0$ and the endpoints $x=-1,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =3(-1)^{4}-8(-1)^{3}+3=14 \\\\ f(0) & =3(0)^{4}-8(0)^{3}+3=3 \\\\ f(1) & =3(1)^{4}-8(1)^{3}+3=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-1)=14,$ so the global maximum is $14.$\n\n- The least value is $f(1)=-2,$ so the global minimum is $-2.$\n\n![](images/9a/9ac7f0c0e28532c897e1c89a35e9c027f614fee40b4b94362a6c5cb012c8a7f6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2106ea68-f48f-5372-87c0-fa8126509655" :knowledge-point/title "Discarding Stationary Points of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14e95874-53a9-59eb-a59d-1506787a86d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446051} {:answer/id #uuid "28e244bd-f5d9-59e7-bae1-37bf7dad0604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446052} {:answer/id #uuid "83b3d4b4-9193-548b-92d2-89f90a26ba3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446057} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0fca65-f9f6-5b4c-986e-f335607b1999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446063} {:answer/id #uuid "cca7c6b4-7bda-5ecf-9402-b6c9fb9f1393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cca7c6b4-7bda-5ecf-9402-b6c9fb9f1393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446065} :answer-field/id #uuid "eafc929c-fdf4-5237-8e6e-4e3e669ade96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d6fccce-a1a6-5495-8484-833c6aab421e" :question/math-academy-id "q-3011" :question/problem "Find the global maximum value of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ on the closed interval $0\\le x\\le 2\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer. We discard all solutions except $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi =\\frac{7\\pi }{4},$ since they are the only values that belong to the given interval.\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{7\\pi }{4},$ and the endpoints $x=0,\\,2\\pi $ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=-1 \\\\ f(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ f(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})=-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ f(2\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2},$ so the global maximum is $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})=-\\sqrt{2},$ so the global minimum is $-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n![](images/76/7645cecb4fef2af4f2e2061752957981414d63700de016ca4a535c8df219597e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2106ea68-f48f-5372-87c0-fa8126509655" :knowledge-point/title "Discarding Stationary Points of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e861644-e02f-5855-8462-b4871cf3e87d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451729} {:answer/id #uuid "6f0520a8-80f6-58e5-9d71-2d0a60dc3c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e861644-e02f-5855-8462-b4871cf3e87d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451729} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cd85ea4-cbeb-58c0-af8e-3fb2f931bca9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be564532-cfe2-5126-b398-a57a31a24c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451731} {:answer/id #uuid "533f6162-a5cb-58c8-a9bd-056be02f39fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "533f6162-a5cb-58c8-a9bd-056be02f39fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451732} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b09ee3a-0d2d-592d-a809-cc23c1a63652" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452713} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "378d5e01-280c-55e9-b40e-4ea9b702b14a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451733} {:answer/id #uuid "ad26f3cb-7963-5bfb-ad32-e409bfa4a927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad26f3cb-7963-5bfb-ad32-e409bfa4a927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451734} :answer-field/id #uuid "712dede4-38c5-58b1-acff-60c9419b0ac6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "199c3a81-6b01-5801-addf-6e540efda73d" :question/math-academy-id "q-79341" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x},$ on the closed interval $-1\\le x\\le 1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The global maximum value is $\\frac{9}{e}$\n- **II.** The global maximum value is $4$\n- **III.** The global minimum value is $e$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2(x-2){e}^{x}+(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =(x-2){e}^{x}[2+x-2] \\\\  & =x(x-2){e}^{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nx(x-2){e}^{x}=0\\,⟹\\,x=0,\\,2.\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,1]$, the critical points are $x=0$ and the endpoints $x=-1,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =(-1-2)^{2}{e}^{-1}=\\frac{9}{e}≈3.31 \\\\ f(0) & =(0-2)^{2}{e}^{0}=4 \\\\ f(1) & =(1-2)^{2}{e}^{1}=e≈2.72\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(0)=4,$ so the global maximum is $4.$\n\n- The least value is $f(1)=e,$ so the global minimum is $e.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"\n\n![](images/ad/adeb7eb92f270a216f30cd0466e91d0363c5a50b17053316e6e9f44d0dfaaf23.png)"}]}
